{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added an `audit_log` table and made every API request that modifies `users` or `feeds` append a row to it. Build and existing tests pass; the new behaviour itself is not covered by any test I could run.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Migration**: new `audit_log` table (`id`, `user_id`, `action`, `table_name`, `row_id`, `created_at`), with no foreign keys so rows outlive deleted users and feeds.\n- **Storage**: `internal/storage/audit.go` adds `AppendAuditLog` and a small feed-count helper, `AuditFeedCount`.\n- **REST API (`internal/api`)**: audit rows on create/update/remove user, create/update/remove/refresh feed, refresh-all and refresh-category, OPML import, and category removal.\n- **Google Reader API (`internal/googlereader`)**: audit rows on subscribe (including quick-add), unsubscribe, rename, move, and disable-tag.\n- **Policy and tags**: `audit_log` added to the `.agentpolicy` nouns of `internal/storage`, `internal/api` and `internal/googlereader`; `@effects` tags updated on the changed functions.\n\nThe last-login update in the auth middleware is left unaudited, as specified.\n\nThings to know:\n- **Not atomic**: the audit row is written in a separate statement after the change succeeds. If the audit insert fails, the request returns 500 but the change stays.\n- **Refresh single feed**: audited before the refresh runs, because a failed refresh still updates the feed's error counters.\n- **Refresh-all / refresh-category**: audited only when at least one job is queued, since the feed rows are updated by background workers.\n- **OPML import**: audited only when the user's feed count actually changed, which also covers imports that fail part-way.\n- **Category removal**: audited only when the category had feeds, because those are deleted by cascade.\n- **Disable-tag (Google Reader)**: always audited on success, even if the removed categories held no feeds.\n- **Bulk operations**: one row per request with `row_id` NULL; Google Reader unsubscribe writes one row per feed.\n\nAssumptions: I t", "t": 1794463273.15}
